From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-b2q: reserve the SPSS region where stock does

The board file deleted sm8350.dtsi's pil_spss_mem and put it back at
0x8b51c000, 1 MiB below stock. Stock reserves 0x8b600000-0x8b700000
(pil_spss_region@8b600000), which is also what sm8350.dtsi has. The
secure processor is started by the bootloader on this phone (stock
"qcom,boot-enabled") and runs from that region, while Linux listed
0x8b61c000-0x8b7fffff as System RAM, so it could allocate pages under
the running SPSS.

Drop the override and keep sm8350.dtsi's node.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts |    6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
index 14313f7..287b433 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
@@ -28,7 +28,6 @@
 /delete-node/ &pil_cvp_mem;
 /delete-node/ &pil_adsp_mem;
 /delete-node/ &pil_slpi_mem;
-/delete-node/ &pil_spss_mem;
 /delete-node/ &rmtfs_mem;
 /delete-node/ &removed_mem;
 
@@ -203,11 +202,6 @@
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		pil_spss_mem: memory@8b51c000 {
-			reg = <0 0x8b51c000 0 0x100000>;
-			no-map;
-		};
-
 		// Should be fine with default?
 		pil_modem_mem: memory@8b800000 {
 			reg = <0 0x8b800000 0 0xf600000>;
